  "query_preview": "..\nAn upper-level ridge over the area will result in warmer than \naverage temperatures through Tuesday. The ridge aloft will \ngradually move to the east beginning tomorrow night ahead of a\nlarge scale upper trough that that will move inland over the west\ncoast. Resulting increasing SW flow aloft will allow for \nanomalous moisture transport into the region.\n\nA shortwave ahead of the main upper trough will move through \neastern Montana Tuesday night and Wednesday with a cold front and \nmixed precipitation and snow at times. Locations north of US-2\ntowards the international border may see snow accumulations \nbetween 0.5\" and 1\" depending on timing of the rain to mixed \nprecipitation and snow transitions. As the main upper trough \nsettles into the intermountain west Wednesday and Thursday cooling\naloft will drive temperatures closer to normal.\n\nLarge scale upper troughing continues across the western US\nthrough the week into next weekend with another distinct upper \nlow moving inland at the end of the work week. This system will \nsee much cooler temperatures, but less moisture. The highest \nprecipitation chances are across southern portions of the \nforecast area. There is a fair amount of uncertainty in the \nquantity and spatial extent of precipitation, however, there is\nmuch higher confidence it will fall as snow rather than rain.\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS:\n\n- Lowered minimum temperatures through Wednesday. Lowered high\n  temperature Wednesday.\n\n- Confidence in fair conditions persisting through Monday is high. \n\n- Confidence in mid week pattern change is high.\n\n- Confidence in precipitation Tuesday night and Wednesday is\n  moderate. Increasing confidence in a transition to snow late\n  Tuesday night into Wednesday morning.",
